{
  "_": "Which eval tasks a change to each file can move: case.py verify's gate 5 and run.py's default --tasks (through fium scope). Patterns are fnmatch globs over repo paths; the first that matches wins. \"*\" means every default task, \"none\" means no live run (a tooling or docs change is re-judged offline: reparse.py and gate.py on runs already kept). A file no rule matches could move anything, so it runs every task. A case's own repro task always runs too, which is how app-screens runs: only when it is the target. A task's own judge files (its tasks/, scorers/ and seeds/ file, and the fixture it reads) move that task: reparse can't re-score them, since final trees aren't kept, and a scorer change needs that task's baseline refreshed. Shared eval code (lib.js, source.py, fixtures/expect.json, and run.py, which wraps every scorer and seeds every page) moves every task; session.py only reads transcripts, which reparse.py redoes offline. A task, scorer, seed or fixture file no task reads yet (a case's new red task) moves none: the case's own repro task runs anyway. gates_test.py keeps these in step with the task definitions and checks every skill file matches a pattern and every task exists.",
